<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umar ibn Awad al-Qu'aiti</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umar ibn Awad al-Qu'aiti was the founder of the fortunes of the Qu'aiti family of Hadramawt in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yafa">Yafa</a>'i tribesman, he rose to high rank as a jamadar, or commander, of the Arab troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. With wealth earned there his family bought land and influence in Hadramawt, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibam">Shibam</a> and Shihr from around 1858, and his descendants ruled the Qu'aiti Sultanate from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukalla">Mukalla</a>.</p></div>
